# `band_span_charge` default-flip vehicle (issue #518) — HEALED, at a WL cost.
# This flow and flow/rnr/mix2.buda are the two corpus vehicles the flip cost.
# History: 0/0/0 pre-flip -> 3/16/1 at the flip (#527/#530) -> 16 opens healed
# by #531/#534, leaving 3 overlaps (issue #535) -> 1 overlap by 2026-08-02 (a
# free ride from later planner/healer work) -> 0/0/0 via the trailing
# `chase_overlaps` refine documented at the end of this script -> 0/0/0 at
# -5.2% detailed WL now, by declaring `healersAhead` (see that line).  The residual
# root cause was the absolute-supply blind spot: the width books say the
# spread bus fits, but DetailedNUTS still needs real SIGNAL tracks at the
# placed position.  See docs/internal/band_span_charge.md.
#
# Uncomment before run_planner to restore the PRE-FLIP endpoint on this flow:
#set_planner_param band_span_charge 0
#
# Deliberately NOT applied: this is a corpus row, and silencing the charging
# model would make the QoR guard stop reporting its known real cost.  The
# `chase_overlaps` fix below is NOT that — it leaves band_span_charge at its
# default and pays the cost visibly in wirelength instead of in overlaps.
#
# Selection-basis lever 3 composition vehicle (the refine_selection docs
# recipe): the PLAIN top-down mix2 pipeline (no healers) ends with triple-digit
# DNUTS opens, and the end-of-flow recipe
#   refine_selection -> negotiate_congestion -> ripup_reroute -> refine_selection
# heals it to a fully clean check_design (0 opens / 0 overlaps, Success).
# The first refine doubles as a healer here BECAUSE the flow is healerless
# until that point: its componentwise accept lets opens/overlap improvements
# through too.  Measured 2026-08-04 with `healersAhead` declared below:
#   run_detailed_nuts   275 opens /  7 ovl
#   refine_selection    167 opens /  0 ovl   (WL 66956 -> 64908)
#   negotiate_congestion 16 opens /  2 ovl
#   ripup_reroute         0 opens /  0 ovl
#   refine_selection      0 opens /  0 ovl   (WL 67972 -> 65339, pure polish)
# Endpoint: abstract WL 65339, detailed WL 793215, check_design Success.
source mix_tracks.buda
open_bdb mix2.bdb.sql
derive_busterms 2
add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
run_hier_bundler depth 2
generate_hier_topologies
# Declares `healersAhead` (like its parent mix2.buda, unlike the five
# `mix2_fast*` siblings, where declaring measured WORSE or WL-negative — each
# carries its own NOTE).  This flow is the one member of that family where the
# declaration WINS, so it takes the win: measured 2026-08-04, QoR holds at
# 0/0/0 while abstract WL drops 68500 -> 65339 (-4.6%), detailed WL
# 836341 -> 793215 (-5.2%), and the flow runs ~20% faster because the healers
# have far less to do.  Comment this line out to restore the undeclared
# trajectory (and with it the issue #535 plateau -- see the note on the
# trailing refine).  See docs/internal/ksegs_default_audit.md.
set_planner_param healersAhead 1
run_planner hier 5 signal_tracks
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
refine_selection
negotiate_congestion
ripup_reroute
# The trailing refine runs in `chase_overlaps` (plain lexicographic accept)
# rather than the default componentwise one — issue #535.  With `healersAhead`
# declared above, the mode no longer MATTERS here: ripup already lands 0/0, so
# this leg is pure WL polish and `refine_selection 30` was measured to reach
# the identical endpoint (same 9 moves / 373 trials, WL 67972 -> 65339).  It is
# kept in `chase_overlaps` form because that is what the UNDECLARED trajectory
# needs, and commenting out the healersAhead line restores it: without the
# declaration the flow stalls after ripup at ONE overlap whose only exit COSTS
# wirelength — refine's winning move is `bundle 62 topo 1->30`, ovl 1->0 at
# wl 68208->68509.  The default accept requires WL strictly lower with
# everything else parity-or-better, so it can never take that move no matter
# how many rounds run (a third and fourth round, and ripup budgets 30/60, were
# all measured byte-identical at 1 overlap), and ripup never reaches topo 30
# either — its trial pool is contention-derived and screened, while refine
# sweeps every eligible bundle's alternates.  That plateau was a SEARCH-
# NEIGHBOURHOOD limit, not a budget or metric one; the declaration dissolves it
# by handing the healers a different (and much easier) starting problem, which
# is a side-step of #535, not a fix for it.
refine_selection 30 chase_overlaps
report_wl
check_design
exit
